# Everything in this repo is a build context for a Linux container, so the
# working tree stays LF on every platform. Without this, a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites the shell scripts and the Containerfile to CRLF
# and they go into the image that way - a CRLF shebang makes the kernel report
# "no such file or directory" for a file that is plainly there, which is how
# this was found: the validator image built cleanly and then refused to start.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.jar  binary
